{
  "about": "Declarative case predicates and the predicates beside them: a case predicate over a key with several records (COLUMN-2), a refused run that keeps the file at its target (OUTPUT-7), a str_extract capture in each expression position, an assertion's predicate and float literals over completed outputs, assertions that read a lookup (CHECK-4, LOOKUP-24), correlated intermediate filters (LOOKUP-7), a single-column key of large integers (LOOKUP-5), and an expression key beside an ill-typed filter (FORMULA-5, LAYER-11). Moved from execution_declarative_case_predicates.rs. A case whose test projected each issue to its phase, condition, rule, spec paths and context, or read some fields of the first issue, names them in compares. A handler ledger is the report's handler rows at SPEC_PATH, NAME and COUNT, the spec_path, handler and count its test compared, and an empty ledger is a kind with no row. The documents assert_lookup_selected (also assert_lookup_empty's specification), assert_lookup_only and dependency_before_bad_filter, with their inputs, are those cases' of case_predicates.json and intermediate_key_reference.json, the truth both installed hosts read; the bytes case_predicates.json states for implicit and assert_lookup_selected are not restated here, and its column_filter and record_filter cases pin the filtered case source. A required match's refusal and a missing lookup field have the phase, condition and rule the registry gives LookupUnmatchedKey and VerificationUnknownReference. An assertion's LIKE over an integer fails with incompatible_input_type (FORMULA-7), a row found among the issues since its test stated none. An intermediate no column reads is pruned with its filter, so its specification saves its one subject with the literal ok in V and V2.",
  "documents": {
    "case_value": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {V: int}}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - name: VALUE\n    type: int\n    derivation:\n      case:\n        - when: \"SRC.V > 0\"\n          then: 7\n        - when: 'FALSE'\n          then: SRC.BAD\n        - otherwise: 8\n",
    "capture": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {V: int}}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "checked": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {V: int}}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - name: VALUE\n    type: int\n    verifications:\n      - allowed_values: {values: [0, 1.0]}\n      - range: {min: 0.0, max: 1.5}\n",
    "assert_lookup_selected": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nbase: SRC\nkeys: [ID, SEQ]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {ID: int, SEQ: int, LIMIT: int}}\n  D: {path: donor.csv, types: {ID: int, TIME: int, X: int}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, SEQ, VALUE]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: P\n    dataset: D\n    key: [ID]\n    filter: 'D.TIME <= SRC.LIMIT'\n    order_by: [D.TIME]\n    keep: last\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: SRC.SEQ}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: int, derivation: P.X}\nverifications:\n  - assert:\n      when: 'P.X IS NOT NULL'\n      require: 'VALUE = P.X AND P.X >= 10'\n",
    "assert_lookup_only": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nbase: SRC\nkeys: [ID, SEQ]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {ID: int, SEQ: int, LIMIT: int}}\n  D: {path: donor.csv, types: {ID: int, TIME: int, X: int}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, SEQ, VALUE]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: P\n    dataset: D\n    key: [ID]\n    filter: 'D.TIME <= SRC.LIMIT'\n    order_by: [D.TIME]\n    keep: last\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: SRC.SEQ}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: int, derivation: 0}\nverifications:\n  - assert:\n      when: 'P.X IS NOT NULL'\n      require: 'P.X >= 10'\n",
    "correlated": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nbase: SRC\nkeys: [ID, SEQ]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: src.csv, types: {ID: int, SEQ: int, CUT: int}}\n  D: {path: donor.csv, types: {ID: int, TIME: int}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, SEQ, A, B]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: P\n    dataset: D\n    key: [ID]\n    filter: \"D.TIME < SRC.CUT\"\n    order_by: [D.TIME]\n    keep: last\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: SRC.SEQ}\n  - {name: A, type: str, derivation: P.A}\n  - {name: B, type: str, derivation: P.B}\n",
    "correlated_source": "ID,SEQ,CUT\n1,1,2\n1,2,4\n3,1,2\n1,3,\n",
    "correlated_donor": "ID,TIME,A,B\n1,1,one,x\n1,3,three,\n2,9,hidden,hidden\n",
    "correlated_alternate": "ID,SEQ,CUT\n1,1,4\n3,1,2\n",
    "single_key": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nbase: SRC\nkeys: [ID]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: src.csv, types: {ID: int}}\n  D: {path: donor.csv, types: {ID: int, SEQ: int}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, A, B]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: P\n    dataset: D\n    key: [ID]\n    order_by: [D.SEQ]\n    keep: first\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: A, type: str, derivation: P.V}\n  - {name: B, type: str, derivation: P.V}\n",
    "dependency_before_bad_filter": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [ID]\ninput:\n  SRC: {path: src.csv, types: {N: int}}\n  TAB: {path: tab.csv, types: {KINT: int, KNUM: float}}\nbase: SRC\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, V, V2]}\nintermediates:\n  - id: LOOK\n    dataset: TAB\n    key: {K: {str_pad: {source: SRC.N, width: 8}}}\n    filter: \"TAB.KINT > 'bad'\"\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: V, type: str, derivation: LOOK.VAL}\n  - {name: V2, type: str, derivation: LOOK.VAL}\n",
    "bad_filter_table": "K,KINT,KNUM,VAL\n\"       7\",7,7,A\n\"     259\",259,259,B\n\"SRC.ABSENT\",9007199254740992,9007199254740992,TEXT\n"
  },
